rns. We might ask Sarah for evidence of B's decision quality or crew cooperation. Or ask Emily for D's temperament impact.\n\nWe need to make a focused argumentative contribution: state current recommendation (likely still C), reference Emily's points, bring new evidence or ask a question.\n\nWe could ask Sarah for any observations of Candidate B's crew cooperation or decision-making in safety-critical situations. That would address missing criteria for B.\n\nThus we will make a public message: I agree with Emily's recommendation for C but note we still lack direct evidence of C's crew cooperation; also we need to compare with B's decision quality. So ask Sarah for B's decision-making evidence.\n\nWe must include metadata vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
